Article 2 (Equipment for Remote Video Trials)
(1) In order to conduct a remote video trial, a courtroom attended by the judge shall be equipped with the following devices:
1. Three color video cameras (one of which shall be used exclusively to film the judge);
2. One color video display device with a diagonal screen length of at least 60 centimeters;
3. Microphones and speakers.
(2) A courtroom not attended by the judge shall be equipped with the following devices:
1. Two color video cameras;
2. One color video display device with a diagonal screen length of at least 100 centimeters that displays only the judge;
3. One color video display device with a diagonal screen length of at least 60 centimeters;
4. Microphones and speakers.
